  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Huo Kong Dong is a lone cultivator who has already joined Chai clan. Fang Yuan, using the name Dong Fang Xiong Ji, says he is old friends with Chai clan’s ninth supreme elder, asks whether that elder has completed the battlefield killer move myriad flash fire, and demands mortal Gu. Huo Kong Dong answers that the ninth elder is still in seclusion. Fang Yuan replies that the elder’s grandfather forced him to stay in after he tried to harass Fairy Yi Yi, then takes the mortal Gu Huo Kong Dong hands over.",
      "chapters": [
        1024
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "after-yi-tian-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_huo_kong_dong",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_mortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan knows the relationship between Chai clan’s ninth elder and Dong Fang Xiong Ji from his previous life at Yi Tian Mountain and the huge gambling contest.",
      "chapters": [
        1025
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "prior-life-memory",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_yi_tian_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Human Smoke Mountain Range has the most living mortals in Southern Border. At its center stands Human Smoke Mountain, the base of Chai clan. The person who created Chai clan was Chai Fu, in his era the number one person in Southern Border’s Gu Immortal world. He cultivated fire path along with earth path, and from The Legends of Ren Zu he gained a human path killer move. Near the end of his life he chose this place, modified the mountain range, and created Human Smoke Mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        1347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-population-strategy",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_human_smoke_mountain",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "char_chai_fu",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chai Fu left the human path method he learned from that book to his descendants. Chai clan focuses on increasing the number of mortals. Those mortals lack Chai clan bloodline and have low aptitude, while highly talented people keep emerging among Chai clan’s own descendants. Limited resources still leave many of those seeds stuck as rank four or five Gu Masters.",
      "chapters": [
        1347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-population-strategy",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the intersection of red dragon river and jade dragon river, Chai clan’s Human Smoke Mountain is north of the whirlpool, Ba clan is south, and Xia clan is east.",
      "chapters": [
        1347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-population-strategy",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ba_clan",
        "fac_xia_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Southern Border’s righteous path has thirteen super clans, and Chai clan is named in that list with Wu, Ba, Shang, Tie, Hou, Luo, Qiao, Xia, Yi, Chi, Yang, and Yao.",
      "chapters": [
        1610
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "super-clan-list",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
